   "title": "AIP-06 · Someone's Thursday, every Thursday",
   "original_idea": "[AIP-06] Someone's Thursday, every Thursday\nReel 9:16 · 20 s · AI implementation & integration · Middle (consideration) · 2026-11-27\n\nObjective:\nDramatise the manual weekly report and show the integrated version: sources joined, numbers agreed, a digest that arrives by itself on Monday morning.\n\nHook (EN):\nEvery Thursday, someone rebuilds this report.\n\nHook (AR):\nكل خميس، يعيد أحدهم بناء هذا التقرير من الصفر.\n\nScene plan:\n0–6 s  Calendar flips Thursday after Thursday; the same Excel file is copied from CRM, ERP and finance by hand (copy-paste animation, three windows).\n6–8 s  'Most companies don't have a software problem. They have a handover problem.'\n8–16 s  The three sources connect with glowing lines into one dashboard; an automated weekly digest lands in the inbox on Monday 8:00.\n16–20 s  '12 systems connected into one source of truth.' End card.\nVisuals: animated HTML windows and dashboard (no real data), Aiphin looking at a holographic chart going up (new pose).\n\nCaption:\nReporting is someone's Thursday, every Thursday, rebuilt from scratch in Excel.\n\nWe join the sources, agree the definitions once, and put the numbers where people check on Monday morning. The person stops being the copy-paste middle and goes back to the work they were hired for.\n\nHashtags:\n#Automation #Integration #Dashboards #Aiphin #Excel\n\nCTA:\nTell us what's slowing you down on WhatsApp +961 71 313 917",
   "input_source": "csv",
