   "title": "AIP-09 · The copy-paste middle",
   "original_idea": "[AIP-09] The copy-paste middle\nCarousel 4:5 · 6 slides · AI implementation & integration · Top (awareness) · 2026-12-04\n\nObjective:\nName the hidden cost of disconnected tools: one person retyping orders, quotes and invoices between systems. Position integration as removing that person from the middle, not replacing them.\n\nHook (EN):\nThere's a person between your systems.\n\nHook (AR):\nهناك شخص عالق بين أنظمتك.\n\nScene plan:\nS1 Hook: illustration of a person between three screens (CRM, ERP, finance).\nS2 'Sales lives in spreadsheets, delivery lives in the ERP, and neither trusts the other's numbers.'\nS3 What they retype: the order, the quote, the invoice, the status update.\nS4 What it costs: hours each week and errors nobody sees until the month closes.\nS5 The fix: CRM, ERP and finance in sync; quote, invoice and approval flows; '4.2 hrs saved per employee each week.'\nS6 'Take the person out of the copy-paste middle.' CTA.\nVisuals: one scene image of an office worker between three monitors (new image prompt), integration diagram built in HTML.\n\nCaption:\nMost companies don't have a software problem. They have a handover problem.\n\nSomewhere in your team there's a person whose real job is copying data from one system into another. We connect the systems so that person can go back to the work only a person can do.\n\nHashtags:\n#Integration #Automation #ERP #CRM #Aiphin\n\nCTA:\nTell us what's slowing you down · WhatsApp +961 71 313 917",
   "input_source": "csv",
   "source_reference": "research/out/aiphin_plan_01.json (Aiphin launch ideas, round 1) › Content › AIP-09",
   "content_type": "carousel",
   "language": "bilingual",
